---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy for Food Scanner, Glasshole and the Scaling Human website, with links to other project policies."
  path="/privacy.html"
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="page-header__kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="page-header__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="page-header__lead">
        This policy covers the free Food Scanner and Glasshole iOS apps published
        under the Scaling Human name and this website. Other projects have
        their own privacy information linked below.
      </p>
    </header>

    <p class="updated">Last updated: October 11, 2026</p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal data. We do not use advertising trackers. The apps
      do not require an account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Food Scanner’s default Local iPhone Vision mode runs on device. Glasshole
      supports Apple Intelligence on compatible devices and runs on device when
      that provider is selected. If you choose a third-party, local-network, or
      custom AI provider, the app sends the content needed for your request to
      that provider using the endpoint and API key you configure.
    </p>

    <h2>Food Scanner</h2>
    <p>
      Food Scanner analyzes food images and generates estimated nutrition
      overlays. Scan history is stored locally on your device. If you choose
      Save to Photos, the app saves the generated result image to your photo
      library.
    </p>
    <p>
      When Local iPhone Vision is selected, food images are classified on device
      and quick nutrition estimates are generated on device from those labels.
      When a third-party, local-network, or custom provider is selected, food
      images are sent to that provider for analysis.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nutrition values are AI estimates for general information only and are not
      medical advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Glasshole</h2>
    <p>
      Glasshole records audio only when you start a session. On-device speech
      recognition converts that audio into text for summarization and
      fact-checking. Audio recordings are not saved. Session history is stored
      locally on your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use the app only with the consent of everyone being recorded and in
      compliance with local laws and regulations where you use it.
    </p>
    <p>
      When Apple Intelligence is selected on a compatible device, processing runs
      on device. When a third-party, local-network, or custom provider is
      selected, transcripts are sent to that provider for summarization and
      fact-checking.
    </p>
    <p>
      AI fact-check results can be wrong and should not be treated as
      authoritative.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional Companion Apps</h2>
    <p>
      Optional companion apps are distributed from GitHub. They connect to the
      iOS apps over your local Wi-Fi or iPhone Personal Hotspot. The Food Scanner
      companion can send food images to the iOS app. The Glasshole companion
      sends activation and stop gestures and displays results from the iOS app.
    </p>

    <h2>Local history and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Both apps save history on your iPhone. Use the history controls to delete
      individual results or clear saved history. Images you save to Photos remain
      in your photo library until you delete them there. Deleting local history
      does not delete copies already sent to a provider or saved elsewhere.
    </p>

    <h2>Choosing an AI provider</h2>
    <p>
      PocketPal mode uses the local endpoint configured in Settings. The default
      is localhost on your iPhone. Ollama and custom endpoints can be on another
      device on your network or on the internet. The destination you configure
      determines where images or transcripts are processed.
    </p>
    <p>
      External providers apply their own privacy and retention policies. Review
      those policies before sending private images or conversations. Changing
      the provider does not remove content already sent to an external service.
    </p>

    <h2>API Keys</h2>
    <p>
      If you configure a third-party AI provider, API keys are stored in the iOS
      Keychain on your device.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The scalinghuman.ai website may use Cloudflare Web Analytics, a
      privacy-oriented product that does not use advertising cookies for
      tracking. It provides aggregate visit and performance metrics (for example page views and
      country). <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/about/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare documents how Web Analytics works</a>. This applies only to the website, not to the iOS apps described
      above.
    </p>

    <h2>Other projects</h2>
    <p>Privacy information is specific to each project:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/apps/rt-library/privacy">RT Library privacy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/apps/book-cricket/privacy">Book Cricket privacy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/apps/ring-local#privacy">Smart Ring Local privacy and project status</a></li>
      <li><a href="/apps/strap-local#privacy">Smart Strap Local privacy and project status</a></li>
      <li><a href="/apps/streaming-devices-kids-meal-mode#family-use">Kids Meal Mode family use and permissions</a></li>
    </ul>

